WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.082
A reshape should be validated.

00:00:02.082 --> 00:00:07.067
For additive measures such as revenue, calculate the total from the source.

00:00:07.067 --> 00:00:10.787
Then calculate the total represented by the pivot cells.

00:00:10.787 --> 00:00:14.672
The totals should agree when the same observations are included.

00:00:14.672 --> 00:00:18.767
This simple check catches many grouping and join mistakes.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:25.872
A pivot converts category values into columns, usually through conditional aggregation in portable SQL.

00:00:25.872 --> 00:00:29.457
Each target column needs a clear aggregation rule.

00:00:29.457 --> 00:00:34.942
Before pivoting, check whether the source contains more than one value for the same row-key and category

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:36.267
combination.
